load @term/seed/code/type/term
  find term

load @term/seed/code/type/multiplicity
  find multiplicity

# The dependent function type, the pi type, the one way the theory forms a type that depends on a value, and the most
# important type former. A function type carries a domain, a multiplicity on the argument (how many times it may be
# used at run time), and a codomain that may MENTION the argument. An ordinary function is the special case where the
# codomain ignores the argument. Below are its four rules in full, the standard formation / introduction / elimination /
# computation shape every type former follows.

# FORMATION: from a domain type A, a multiplicity rho, and a codomain type B that may use a variable of A, form the pi
# type. It inhabits the maximum of A's and B's universe, except at the impredicative bottom where a pi into Type 0 stays
# in Type 0 whatever the domain's level. This is the rule that builds the type.
form function-type
  link domain, like term
  link usage, like multiplicity
  link codomain, like term

# INTRODUCTION: a lambda abstraction. Given a body that inhabits the codomain B under a fresh variable of the domain A,
# the lambda inhabits the pi type. This is how a function is built: by saying what it does to its argument.
form lambda-abstraction
  link body, like term

# ELIMINATION: application. A term of the pi type applied to an argument of the domain A yields a term of the codomain B
# with the argument substituted in. This is how a function is used.
form function-application
  link target, like term
  link input, like term

# COMPUTATION (beta): applying a lambda to an argument reduces to the body with the argument substituted for the bound
# variable. Beta is the engine of normalization, the rule that actually runs a function.
form beta-reduction
  link redex, like function-application

# UNIQUENESS (eta): a function equals the lambda that applies it to a fresh variable, so two functions agreeing on every
# argument are equal. With observational equality this eta law computes, giving function extensionality for free.
form eta-law
  link function, like term
